WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.088
Why start here?

2
00:00:01.088 --> 00:00:02.700
Because the order matters.

3
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:08.104
If approval for privileged roles is switched
on before working emergency accounts

4
00:00:08.104 --> 00:00:12.582
exist, you can lock everyone out:
every administrator role is eligible,

5
00:00:12.582 --> 00:00:15.825
approval is required, and
nobody is left to approve.

6
00:00:15.825 --> 00:00:17.854
That's the documented lockout,

7
00:00:17.854 --> 00:00:21.588
and it's why Book 04 makes this
step the one that can't move.

8
00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:24.444
The emergency accounts
are also the program's

9
00:00:24.444 --> 00:00:26.925
main exception to zero standing access.

10
00:00:26.925 --> 00:00:29.494
The inventory in Chapter
1 lets them through

11
00:00:29.494 --> 00:00:31.925
only because they're listed as exceptions.

12
00:00:31.925 --> 00:00:34.560
This chapter makes sure
that exception is real.
